WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.666 --> 00:00:03.333
(drums rolling)

00:00:07.449 --> 00:00:10.282
- God sent me here to be a cowboy.

00:00:11.442 --> 00:00:13.226
And the first thing a lady told me, said,

00:00:13.226 --> 00:00:16.385
‘When you rode in the arena,
you said, ‘Everybody's eyes

00:00:16.385 --> 00:00:17.468
were on you.’”

00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:23.090
And she said, ‘Half of
‘em wanted you to win,

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.898
but the other half don't give
a damn if you win or not,

00:00:26.898 --> 00:00:29.815
because of the color of your skin.'

00:00:30.922 --> 00:00:34.133
But, I'll always want to win.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.807
(electric guitar strums)

00:00:37.807 --> 00:00:41.307
I'd been a professional cowboy since 1959.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:46.806
Dealing with racism back in
the ’50's and ’60's and now,

00:00:46.806 --> 00:00:48.806
it's still kind of hard.

00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:52.382
People would see me at a rodeo,

00:00:52.382 --> 00:00:54.638
and because I was of a different color,

00:00:54.638 --> 00:00:57.971
they thought I was, uh, working for somebody.

00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:02.022
People want to know, a lot of times:

00:01:02.022 --> 00:01:04.238
Why did you want to be a calf roper?

00:01:04.238 --> 00:01:08.405
Well, I had seen a lot of black
cowboys judged improperly,

00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:12.030
but in the calf roping,

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.614
I knew that I wasn't going
to be judged by a human,

00:01:14.614 --> 00:01:17.239
I was going to be judged by the clock.

00:01:17.239 --> 00:01:20.030
The clock was going to determine
whether I get any money,

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:20.863
or not.

00:01:25.494 --> 00:01:29.661
Right now, all I do is put
on Cowboys of Color rodeos.

00:01:30.815 --> 00:01:35.335
Cowboys of Color features
Indians, Blacks, Hispanics

00:01:35.335 --> 00:01:37.252
and white cowboys also.

00:01:39.263 --> 00:01:43.537
Black cowboys in the history
books is damn near forgotten.

00:01:43.537 --> 00:01:46.101
Very many people don't even realize

00:01:46.101 --> 00:01:50.085
that New Mexico was
discovered by a black man.

00:01:50.085 --> 00:01:53.002
Chicago was founded by a black man.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.997
I don't care what color you are,

00:01:55.997 --> 00:01:59.205
these are the kind of things
that we want young people

00:01:59.205 --> 00:02:00.038
to know.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:08.753
I have four boys, they are
all professional cowboys.

00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:13.026
My granddaughter, Rachel Hern,
this was her first big rodeo.

00:02:13.026 --> 00:02:15.526
So, it's a way of life for us.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.498
I'm 76 years old.

00:02:20.498 --> 00:02:24.139
That's pretty darn old for a cowboy.

00:02:24.139 --> 00:02:25.241
It's in my blood.

00:02:25.241 --> 00:02:29.672
I think, the day that I lay
down and can't breathe anymore,

00:02:29.672 --> 00:02:31.577
I'll still be looking for a rodeo.

00:02:31.577 --> 00:02:34.244
(banjo playing)

